R"],["to graduate","obtenir son diplôme","ohp-tuh-NEER sohn dee-PLOHM"]]}],"grammar":[{"id":"pronouns","title":"Pronouns","text":["Je becomes j' before a vowel: j'ai, j'habite. On is very common in speech and means \"we\"."],"rows":[["I","je","zhuh"],["you (informal)","tu","too"],["he / she","il / elle","eel / el"],["we","nous","noo"],["you (formal or plural)","vous","voo"],["they","ils / elles","eel / el"],["one, we (casual)","on","ohn"]],"ex":[["I am a student","je suis étudiant","zhuh swee zay-tew-DYAHN"],["you are tall","tu es grand","too ay GRAHN"],["she is my sister","elle est ma sœur","el ay mah SUR"],["we are friends","nous sommes amis","noo som zah-MEE"],["they are teachers","ils sont professeurs","eel sohn proh-feh-SUR"]]},{"id":"singular-and-plural","title":"Singular and plural","text":["Most plurals add -s, but the s is silent. You hear the plural in the article: le → les, un → des. Words ending in -al change to -aux. Words in -eau add -x."],"rows":[["the (m / f, singular)","le / la","luh / lah"],["the (plural)","les","lay"],["a (m / f)","un / une","uhn / oon"],["some (plural)","des","day"]],"ex":[["one cat, two cats","un chat, deux chats","uhn SHAH duh SHAH"],["the book, the books","le livre, les livres","luh LEE-vruh lay LEE-vruh"],["a girl, girls","une fille, des filles","oon FEE day FEE"],["the horse, the horses","le cheval, les chevaux","luh shuh-VAHL lay shuh-VOH"],["the coat, the coats","le manteau, les manteaux","luh mahn-TOH lay mahn-TOH"]]},{"id":"tre-to-be","title":"Être: to be","text":[],"rows":[["I am","je suis","zhuh SWEE"],["you are","tu es","too AY"],["he / she is","il / elle est","eel / el AY"],["we are","nous sommes","noo SOM"],["you all are","vous êtes","voo ZET"],["they are","ils / elles sont","eel / el SOHN"]],"ex":[["I am English","je suis anglais","zhuh swee zahn-GLAY"],["he is a doctor","il est médecin","eel ay mayd-SAN"],["we are tired","nous sommes fatigués","noo som fah-tee-GAY"],["are you from Paris?","tu es de Paris ?","too ay duh pah-REE"],["they are at home","ils sont à la maison","eel sohn ah lah may-ZOHN"]]},{"id":"avoir-to-have","title":"Avoir: to have","text":["Avoir is also used for age (j'ai seize ans), hunger and thirst (j'ai faim, j'ai soif)."],"rows":[["I have","j'ai","zhay"],["you have","tu as","too AH"],["he / she has","il / elle a","eel / el AH"],["we have","nous avons","noo zah-VOHN"],["you all have","vous avez","voo zah-VAY"],["they have","ils / elles ont","eel / el ZOHN"]],"ex":[["I have a brother","j'ai un frère","zhay uhn FRAIR"],["she has two cats","elle a deux chats","el ah duh SHAH"],["we have time","nous avons le temps","noo zah-VOHN luh TAHN"],["I am hungry","j'ai faim","zhay FAN"],["they have a car","ils ont une voiture","eel zohn oon vwah-TEWR"]]},{"id":"regular-verbs-present-tense","title":"Regular verbs (present tense)","text":["-er verbs, the biggest group. Drop -er, add: -e, -es, -e, -ons, -ez, -ent. The -e, -es, -ent endings are silent."],"rows":[["parler: je","parle","parl"],["tu","parles","parl"],["il / elle","parle","parl"],["nous","parlons","par-LOHN"],["vous","parlez","par-LAY"],["ils / elles","parlent","parl"]],"ex":[["I speak English","je parle anglais","zhuh parl ahn-GLAY"],["you live in Paris","tu habites à Paris","too ah-BEET ah pah-REE"],["she works a lot","elle travaille beaucoup","el trah-VY boh-KOO"],["we eat bread","nous mangeons du pain","noo mahn-ZHOHN dew PAN"],["they like music","ils aiment la musique","eel zem lah mew-ZEEK"]]},{"id":"aller-to-go","title":"Aller: to go","text":["Going to do something soon: aller + infinitive. Je vais manger = I am going to eat."],"rows":[["I go","je vais","zhuh VAY"],["you go","tu vas","too VAH"],["he / she goes","il / elle va","eel / el VAH"],["we go","nous allons","noo zah-LOHN"],["you all go","vous allez","voo zah-LAY"],["they go","ils / elles vont","eel / el VOHN"]],"ex":[["I am going to school","je vais à l'école","zhuh vay zah lay-KOL"],["where are you going?","tu vas où ?","too vah OO"],["we are going to eat","nous allons manger","noo zah-lohn mahn-ZHAY"],["she is going to travel","elle va voyager","el vah vwah-yah-ZHAY"],["let's go!","on y va !","ohn ee VAH"]]},{"id":"basic-sentences","title":"Basic sentences","text":["Order: subject, verb, rest. Adjectives usually come after the noun, but short common ones (grand, petit, bon, beau, nouveau, vieux) come before."],"rows":[["subject + verb + rest","Je mange du pain.","zhuh mahnzh dew PAN"],["adjective after noun","une voiture rouge","oon vwah-TEWR ROOZH"],["short adjective before","un petit chat","uhn puh-TEE SHAH"]],"ex":[["I eat bread","je mange du pain","zhuh mahnzh dew PAN"],["Marie reads a book","Marie lit un livre","mah-REE lee uhn LEE-vruh"],["we live in a big house","nous habitons une grande maison","noo zah-bee-TOHN oon grahnd may-ZOHN"],["he works here today","il travaille ici aujourd'hui","eel trah-VY ee-SEE oh-zhoor-DWEE"],["the dog is black","le chien est noir","luh SHYAN ay NWAHR"]]},{"id":"negation","title":"Negation","text":["Wrap the verb: ne ... pas. In speech, ne is often dropped: je sais pas. Before a vowel: n'.","Wrap the verb with ne ... pas: je ne parle pas. Also ne ... rien (nothing), ne ... personne (nobody), ne ... jamais (never). Before a vowel ne becomes n'. In speech ne is often dropped."],"rows":[["not","ne ... pas","nuh ... pah"],["never","ne ... jamais","nuh ... zhah-MAY"],["nothing","ne ... rien","nuh ... RYAN"],["nobody","ne ... personne","nuh ... pair-SUN"],["no more","ne ... plus","nuh ... PLEW"],["ne ... pas","je ne parle pas","zhuh nuh parl pah"],["nothing","ne ... rien","nuh ree-AN"],["nobody","ne ... personne","nuh pair-SUN"],["never","ne ... jamais","nuh zhah-MAY"]],"ex":[["I want","je veux","zhuh vuh"],["I do not want","je ne veux pas","zhuh nuh vuh pah"],["I speak English","je parle anglais","zhuh parl ahn-GLAY"],["I do not speak English","je ne parle pas anglais","zhuh nuh parl pah ahn-GLAY"],["I like it","ça me plaît","sah muh play"],["I do not like it","ça ne me plaît pas","sah nuh muh play pah"],["she is here","elle est ici","el ay ee-SEE"],["she is not here","elle n'est pas ici","el nay pah zee-SEE"],["I have a car","j'ai une voiture","zhay ewn vwah-TEWR"],["I do not have a car","je n'ai pas de voiture","zhuh nay pah duh vwah-TEWR"],["I understand","je comprends","zhuh kohn-PRAHN"],["I do not understand","je ne comprends pas","zhuh nuh kohn-PRAHN pah"],["we are tired","nous sommes fatigués","noo sum fah-tee-GAY"],["we are not tired","nous ne sommes pas fatigués","noo nuh sum pah fah-tee-GAY"],["he works on Sundays","il travaille le dimanche","eel trah-VY luh dee-MAHNSH"],["he does not work on Sundays","il ne travaille pas le dimanche","eel nuh trah-VY pah luh dee-MAHNSH"]]},{"id":"asking-questions","title":"Asking questions","text":["Three ways: raise your voice (friendly), put est-ce que before the sentence (neutral), or swap verb and pronoun (formal)."],"rows":[["rising voice","Tu parles anglais ?","too parl ahn-GLAY"],["est-ce que","Est-ce que tu parles anglais ?","es kuh too parl ahn-GLAY"],["swap (formal)","Parlez-vous anglais ?","par-lay-VOO ahn-GLAY"]],"ex":[["do you speak English?","tu parles anglais ?","too parl ahn-GLAY"],["is she a doctor?","est-ce qu'elle est médecin ?","es kel ay mayd-SAN"],["do you have a pen?","tu as un stylo ?","too ah uhn stee-LOH"],["are you tired?","vous êtes fatigué ?","voo zet fah-tee-GAY"],["is it far?","est-ce que c'est loin ?","es kuh say LWAN"]]},{"id":"question-words","title":"Question words","text":[],"rows":[["what","que / quoi","kuh / KWAH"],["who","qui","KEE"],["where","où","OO"],["when","quand","KAHN"],["why","pourquoi","poor-KWAH"],["how","comment","koh-MAHN"],["which","quel","KEL"],["how much / how many","combien","kohm-BYAN"]],"ex":[["what is this?","qu'est-ce que c'est ?","kess kuh SAY"],["who is she?","qui est-elle ?","kee ay-TEL"],["where do you live?","où habites-tu ?","oo ah-beet-TOO"],["when is the exam?","quand est l'examen ?","kahn ay leg-zah-MAN"],["why are you late?","pourquoi es-tu en retard ?","poor-kwah ay-TOO ahn ruh-TAHR"],["how much is it?","c'est combien ?","say kohm-BYAN"]]},{"id":"possessives","title":"Possessives","text":[],"rows":[["my (m / f / plural)","mon / ma / mes","mohn / mah / may"],["your (informal)","ton / ta / tes","tohn / tah / tay"],["his / her","son / sa / ses","sohn / sah / say"],["our","notre / nos","NOH-truh / noh"],["your (formal)","votre / vos","VOH-truh / voh"],["their","leur / leurs","LUR"]],"ex":[["my house","ma maison","mah may-ZOHN"],["your friends","tes amis","tay zah-MEE"],["his sister","sa sœur","sah SUR"],["our teacher","notre professeur","NOH-truh proh-feh-SUR"],["your name (formal)","votre nom","VOH-truh NOHN"]]},{"id":"formal-vs-informal","title":"Formal vs informal","text":["tu / ton / te for friends and family. vous / votre for strangers and work. With vous, the verb ends -ez."],"rows":[["you, informal","tu","too"],["you, formal","vous","voo"],["your, informal","ton / ta / tes","tohn / tah / tay"],["your, formal","votre / vos","VOH-truh / voh"]],"ex":[["you speak (informal)","tu parles","too parl"],["you speak (formal)","vous parlez","voo par-LAY"],["how are you? (informal)","comment vas-tu ?","koh-mahn vah-TOO"],["how are you? (formal)","comment allez-vous ?","koh-mahn tah-lay VOO"],["thank you (formal)","merci, madame","mair-SEE mah-DAHM"]]},{"id":"past-and-future-simple","title":"Past and future (simple)","text":["Past: avoir (or être) + past participle: j'ai parlé, je suis allé. Future: aller + infinitive, or add -ai, -as, -a, -ons, -ez, -ont to the infinitive."],"rows":[["I spoke","j'ai parlé","zhay par-LAY"],["I ate","j'ai mangé","zhay mahn-ZHAY"],["I went","je suis allé","zhuh swee zah-LAY"],["I will speak","je parlerai","zhuh par-luh-RAY"]],"ex":[["yesterday I worked","hier j'ai travaillé","yair zhay trah-vah-YAY"],["she bought a book","elle a acheté un livre","el ah ahsh-TAY uhn LEE-vruh"],["I went home","je suis rentré à la maison","zhuh swee rahn-TRAY ah lah may-ZOHN"],["I will call you tomorrow","je t'appellerai demain","zhuh tah-pel-RAY duh-MAN"],["we will eat at eight","nous mangerons à huit heures","noo mahnzh-ROHN ah weet UR"]]},{"id":"commands","title":"Commands","text":["Use the tu or vous form without the pronoun: parle ! (tu), parlez ! (vous), parlons ! (let us). -er verbs lose the final -s in the tu form (tu parles → parle). Negative: ne ... pas around the verb."],"rows":[["speak! (tu)","parle !","parl"],["speak! (vous)","parlez !","par-LAY"],["let us speak!","parlons !","par-LOHN"]],"ex":[["come here","viens ici","vee-AN ee-SEE"],["do not come here","ne viens pas ici","nuh vee-AN pah zee-SEE"],["sit down","assieds-toi","ah-see-AY twah"],["do not sit down","ne t'assieds pas","nuh tah-see-AY pah"],["be quiet","tais-toi","tay twah"],["do not be late","ne sois pas en retard","nuh swah pah zahn ruh-TAR"],["open the door","ouvre la porte","oovr lah port"],["close the window","ferme la fenêtre","fairm lah fuh-NETR"],["listen to me","écoute-moi","ay-KOOT mwah"],["do not worry","ne t'inquiète pas","nuh tan-kee-ET pah"],["speak slowly","parle lentement","parl lahnt-MAHN"],["wait a moment","attends un moment","ah-TAHN uhn moh-MAHN"]]},{"id":"can-must-want","title":"Can, must, want","text":["pouvoir (can), devoir (must), vouloir (want) + infinitive: je peux nager, nous devons partir, je veux manger. Il ne faut pas = you must not."],"rows":[["I can","je peux","zhuh puh"],["I must","je dois","zhuh dwah"],["I want","je veux","zhuh vuh"]],"ex":[["I can swim","je sais nager","zhuh say nah-ZHAY"],["I cannot swim","je ne sais pas nager","zhuh nuh say pah nah-ZHAY"],["can you help me?","tu peux m'aider ?","tew puh may-DAY"],["we must go","nous devons partir","noo duh-VOHN par-TEER"],["we must not go","nous ne devons pas partir","noo nuh duh-VOHN pah par-TEER"],["I want to eat","je veux manger","zhuh vuh mahn-ZHAY"],["I do not want to eat","je ne veux pas manger","zhuh nuh vuh pah mahn-ZHAY"],["you can come","tu peux venir","tew puh vuh-NEER"],["you cannot come","tu ne peux pas venir","tew nuh puh pah vuh-NEER"],["she wants to study","elle veut étudier","el vuh ay-tew-dee-AY"],["I must work today","je dois travailler aujourd'hui","zhuh dwah trah-vah-YAY oh-zhoor-DWEE"],["you must not run","il ne faut pas courir","eel nuh foh pah koo-REER"]]},{"id":"in-on-at","title":"In, on, at","text":["à = at / to; dans = in; sur = on; sous = under; à côté de = next to; près de = near; à neuf heures = at nine."],"rows":[["on","sur","sewr"],["under","sous","soo"],["next to","à côté de","ah koh-TAY duh"],["near","près de","pray duh"]],"ex":[["the book is on the table","le livre est sur la table","luh LEEVR ay sewr lah TABL"],["the cat is under the table","le chat est sous la table","luh shah ay soo lah TABL"],["I am at school","je suis à l'école","zhuh swee zah lay-KOHL"],["I am at home","je suis à la maison","zhuh swee zah lah may-ZOHN"],["the shop is next to the bank","le magasin est à côté de la banque","luh mah-gah-ZAN ay tah koh-TAY duh lah bahnk"],["the park is near the station","le parc est près de la gare","luh park ay pray duh lah gar"],["we meet in the morning","on se voit le matin","ohn suh vwah luh mah-TAN"],["the lesson is at nine","le cours est à neuf heures","luh koor ay tah nuh-VUHR"],["the key is in the bag","la clé est dans le sac","lah klay ay dahn luh sahk"]]},{"id":"comparing-things","title":"Comparing things","text":["plus + adjective + que = more than (plus grand que). moins... que = less than. le plus... = the most. meilleur = better, pire = worse."],"rows":[["bigger than","plus grand que","plew grahn kuh"],["better","meilleur","may-YUHR"],["the biggest","le plus grand","luh plew grahn"]],"ex":[["big, bigger, the biggest","grand, plus grand, le plus grand","grahn plew grahn luh plew grahn"],["small, smaller, the smallest","petit, plus petit, le plus petit","puh-TEE plew puh-TEE luh plew puh-TEE"],["this is better than that","c'est meilleur que ça","say may-YUHR kuh sah"],["this is worse than that","c'est pire que ça","say peer kuh sah"],["she is taller than me","elle est plus grande que moi","el ay plew grahnd kuh mwah"],["Tashkent is bigger than Samarkand","Tachkent est plus grand que Samarcande","tahsh-KENT ay plew grahn kuh sah-mar-KAHND"],["it is the cheapest","c'est le moins cher","say luh mwan shair"],["the same as","pareil que","pah-RAY kuh"]]},{"id":"everyday-sentences","title":"Everyday sentences","text":["Extra practice with the most useful patterns."],"rows":[],"ex":[["he is a teacher","il est professeur","eel ay proh-feh-SUHR"],["you (plural) are students","vous êtes étudiants","voo zet ay-tew-dee-AHN"],["I am happy","je suis content","zhuh swee kohn-TAHN"],["she is at school","elle est à l'école","el ay tah lay-KOHL"],["you are my friend","tu es mon ami","tew ay mohn nah-MEE"],["it is cold","il fait froid","eel fay frwah"],["I study English","j'étudie l'anglais","zhay-tew-DEE lahn-GLAY"],["he teaches maths","il enseigne les maths","eel ahn-SAYN-yuh lay mahth"],["they work every day","ils travaillent tous les jours","eel trah-VY-yuh too lay zhoor"],["is this your book?","c'est ton livre ?","say tohn LEEVR"],["are they here?","ils sont ici ?","eel sohn tee-SEE"],["do you like tea?","tu aimes le thé ?","tew em luh tay"],["what time is it?","quelle heure est-il ?","kel uhr ay-TEEL"],["whose book is this?","c'est le livre de qui ?","say luh LEEVR duh kee"],["how old are you?","quel âge as-tu ?","kel ahzh ah-TEW"],["how do you say it?","comment on dit ça ?","koh-MAHN ohn dee sah"],["your book (formal)","votre livre","VOH-truh LEEVR"],["their house","leur maison","luhr may-ZOHN"],["my phone","mon téléphone","mohn tay-lay-FOHN"],["excuse me, sir","excusez-moi, monsieur","ek-skew-ZAY mwah muh-SYUH"],["please sit down (formal)","asseyez-vous, s'il vous plaît","ah-say-YAY voo seel voo play"],["come here (informal)","viens ici","vee-AN ee-SEE"],["yesterday I was tired","hier j'étais fatigué","ee-YAIR zhay-TAY fah-tee-GAY"],["I will study tomorrow","j'étudierai demain","zhay-tew-dee-uh-RAY duh-MAN"],["we went to the park","nous sommes allés au parc","noo sum zah-LAY oh park"]]}],"name":"French","id":"fr","flag":"fr","note":""}